00:12.853 --> 00:15.689
- I'm home.
- Welcome back!

00:17.358 --> 00:19.693
- What's wrong, Iori?
- Are you hung over?

00:19.860 --> 00:21.195
Go throw up in the toilet.

00:21.362 --> 00:23.614
It's because you're dressed like that!

00:26.242 --> 00:27.952
Oh, you mean this?

00:28.244 --> 00:30.871
We're going diving later. We were preparing.

00:31.038 --> 00:33.499
We have swimsuits on underneath.

00:33.666 --> 00:35.960
Oh, I see...

00:36.126 --> 00:38.462
Can I talk to you three for a second?

00:39.713 --> 00:41.966
You liars!

00:43.050 --> 00:46.887
Be passionate, my friends

00:47.096 --> 00:50.057
Shine bright with the sun

00:50.266 --> 00:53.686
Dive into the blue sky

00:53.894 --> 00:57.982
And let summer take it all

01:01.193 --> 01:04.530
Grand Blue Dreaming

01:11.787 --> 01:15.624
Be passionate, my friends

01:15.833 --> 01:18.877
Shine bright with the sun

01:19.086 --> 01:22.172
Dive into the blue sky

01:22.381 --> 01:26.427
And let summer take it all

01:26.635 --> 01:29.430
An expanding ocean of possibilities

01:29.638 --> 01:33.475
Summer is our amore

01:33.684 --> 01:37.146
We’ll swear to the crystal clear sky

01:37.354 --> 01:40.274
Summer is in our hands

01:40.482 --> 01:44.361
Be passionate, my friends

01:44.570 --> 01:47.531
Shine bright with the sun

01:47.740 --> 01:50.993
Dive into the blue sky

01:51.201 --> 01:54.621
And let summer take it all

01:54.830 --> 01:58.792
With a cheerful heart

01:59.001 --> 02:01.795
Don’t mess with me

02:02.004 --> 02:05.257
Keep going even if you fall

02:05.466 --> 02:09.094
And let summer take it all

02:12.097 --> 02:14.558
It's about today's guests...

02:14.725 --> 02:16.560
Oh, welcome back.

02:17.811 --> 02:20.356
So you're wearing clothes, huh...

02:21.148 --> 02:24.818
- What's wrong?
- Something came up. The guests want to postpone.

02:25.277 --> 02:28.697
- That's too bad.
- So, today's canceled?

02:28.947 --> 02:31.575
Too bad. Let's put on clothes for once.

02:31.742 --> 02:34.286
People usually wear clothes all the time...

02:35.871 --> 02:37.164
Well, then...

02:37.331 --> 02:38.832
Thank you for the meal!

02:39.208 --> 02:42.086
We have some free time before drinking tonight.

02:42.419 --> 02:44.088
Yeah. You're right.

02:44.630 --> 02:47.007
Iori, what are you going to do?

02:47.174 --> 02:48.967
Why are you asking me?

02:49.134 --> 02:51.220
Do you have something else planned?

02:51.387 --> 02:53.847
I'm saying I'm not going drinking today.

02:54.014 --> 02:56.225
You know what kind of club this is, right?

02:56.392 --> 02:58.477
This is a diving club, right?

02:58.936 --> 03:00.229
Iori!

03:00.396 --> 03:02.022
Yes?

03:02.314 --> 03:05.192
This is your third day here. Do you even know?

03:06.527 --> 03:07.861
Know what?

03:08.028 --> 03:09.988
Where your room is.

03:12.866 --> 03:14.993
- Now that you mention it...
- Right?

03:15.661 --> 03:20.624
I know you want to have fun in college,
but you can't stay out three nights in a row.

03:20.833 --> 03:24.128
You're right. You're right, Nanaka.

03:24.586 --> 03:27.381
Anyway, that's why I'm not going tonight.

03:27.714 --> 03:29.299
It can't be helped.

03:29.466 --> 03:31.385
Iori's not going...

03:31.593 --> 03:34.388
I'm really sorry.

03:34.596 --> 03:35.806
It's okay.

03:35.973 --> 03:38.142
We have enough people anyway.

03:39.351 --> 03:43.021
We're drinking with girls from
Oumi Women's University tonight.

03:45.983 --> 03:48.152
Did you say... a women's university?

03:50.195 --> 03:53.031
What do you want to do until we go drinking?

03:55.200 --> 03:57.619
I'm begging you! Let me go!

03:59.121 --> 04:01.039
Hey, Iori! What happened?

04:01.623 --> 04:05.544
I remember which club I joined!

04:05.711 --> 04:07.379
- Diving, right?
- No!

04:07.546 --> 04:09.798
I didn't join a diving club!

04:10.132 --> 04:12.176
What a quick change of heart.

04:12.342 --> 04:14.428
So quick it almost snapped off.

04:14.636 --> 04:16.430
Please, Nanaka!

04:16.930 --> 04:20.267
Why don't you get up and put on some clothes first?

04:20.601 --> 04:22.686
Why do you take off your clothes anyway?

04:22.895 --> 04:25.063
To show people I'm a straightforward guy!

04:25.355 --> 04:27.316
I know you want to have fun...

04:27.483 --> 04:28.567
Captain!

04:28.775 --> 04:30.903
- No!
- Please!

04:31.069 --> 04:32.654
No means no!

04:34.114 --> 04:36.575
How can I get her to let me go?

04:36.783 --> 04:39.036
She was pretty firm. You should give up.

04:39.203 --> 04:41.538
No! I won't give up!

04:41.705 --> 04:44.958
What's causing you to be so persistent?

04:45.167 --> 04:48.712
- I'm ashamed to admit it's my sex drive.
- That is embarrassing.

04:49.087 --> 04:52.341
That doesn't matter. How can I convince Nanaka?

04:54.468 --> 04:56.470
You should finish unpacking first.

04:56.845 --> 04:59.473
- But that won't be enough...
- Not enough?

04:59.640 --> 05:04.436
Then you just have to decorate your room in a way
that says you're an independent man.

05:04.895 --> 05:07.689
- Easier said than done...
- It can't be helped.

05:08.148 --> 05:11.193
Let me give you a hand.

05:11.360 --> 05:16.365
I'll transform your room
into the room of an adult man!

05:17.533 --> 05:19.368
Did you finish unpacking already?

05:19.535 --> 05:23.747
Yes! I'm an independent adult, you know.

05:38.053 --> 05:40.597
No! Nanaka, this isn't--

05:42.933 --> 05:46.520
- Well, you are a guy, after all...
- No, wait--

05:49.314 --> 05:51.275
- How was it, Iori?
- Perfect, right?

05:51.441 --> 05:53.485
You jerks!

05:54.361 --> 05:58.031
- It wasn't a success?
- How could anyone ever think this would succeed!?

05:58.323 --> 06:02.703
When a mom finds her son's porn,
she thinks, "He's grown up!" Right?

06:02.869 --> 06:04.871
That's totally different!

06:05.038 --> 06:06.665
Then what do you want us to do?

06:06.873 --> 06:12.546
Just make it normal! A normal room for a college student
living alone for the first time!

06:12.754 --> 06:14.548
What? That's all you wanted?

06:14.715 --> 06:16.675
You should've said something first.

06:17.718 --> 06:19.553
I shouldn't have asked you.

06:19.720 --> 06:23.432
I'll do the rest myself. Take these with you and leave.

06:23.599 --> 06:26.810
- So, we can put these away?
- Of course!

06:27.269 --> 06:32.941
Kotobuki and I wanted to give you one
to congratulate you for entering college.

06:37.821 --> 06:40.699
Iori, I was going to throw this away, but if you want it...

06:40.907 --> 06:43.201
Oh, yes! Oh, yes! Yes!

06:43.410 --> 06:46.330
Pretty good. 78 points.

06:47.581 --> 06:49.583
I was sure you'd like it.

06:49.875 --> 06:53.754
It's so good! It's so good!

06:54.338 --> 06:56.590
She got the wrong idea because of you.

06:56.757 --> 06:58.508
I don't think so.

06:58.675 --> 07:01.845
Who says "Do you want to watch this together?"

07:02.012 --> 07:05.182
Just leave! And leave the present!

07:05.349 --> 07:09.061
- Wait, Iori.
- We can't just leave you hanging like this.

07:09.227 --> 07:12.356
- No. I've had enough.
- How about another one?

07:13.815 --> 07:15.442
I'll believe you guys.

07:15.901 --> 07:16.943
Leave it to us.

07:17.110 --> 07:21.073
- We'll make your room perfect for a freshman.
- I'm counting on you.

07:23.325 --> 07:27.079
Iori. Chisa looked mad just now. What happened?

07:27.496 --> 07:31.083
I was the only one who got a
housewarming gift from my seniors.

07:31.583 --> 07:34.711
She was mad about that? She's still immature.

07:35.003 --> 07:37.798
I asked her if she wanted to watch it together, but...

07:37.964 --> 07:39.466
Oh, Iori.

07:39.633 --> 07:41.968
Nanaka! I can explain!

07:42.302 --> 07:44.304
It's okay. I don't mind.

07:44.638 --> 07:47.015
I called my friend just now.

07:47.182 --> 07:49.851
She said it's normal for a guy your age.

07:50.018 --> 07:52.854
You're giving me a bad reputation.

07:53.188 --> 07:56.274
- My seniors were playing a joke on me.
- I see.

07:56.441 --> 07:59.111
Yes. The room is totally normal now.

07:59.444 --> 08:03.073
- Thanks for the tape.
- No problem.

08:11.915 --> 08:12.999
Hey.

08:13.583 --> 08:16.628
What do you think? I designed this room.

08:17.295 --> 08:19.005
What are you doing here?

08:19.172 --> 08:22.884
How dare you rip up my excellent solo-life starter set?

08:23.051 --> 08:26.513
Shut up! You ruined my room with your bad taste!

08:26.930 --> 08:30.267
I spent so much time copying those posters!

08:30.434 --> 08:32.269
Curse you and your descendants!

08:32.561 --> 08:36.231
All I did was rip some copies.
My descendants don't deserve to be cursed.

08:37.107 --> 08:39.443
It's perfect this time, right?

08:39.609 --> 08:43.530
Who better to decorate
a freshman room than a freshman?

08:43.697 --> 08:48.160
- This is totally out of the question!
- Then what kind of a room do you want?

08:48.326 --> 08:50.787
The exact opposite of this!

08:51.955 --> 08:53.665
Oh, really?

08:53.832 --> 08:55.667
You should have said something first.

08:55.834 --> 08:57.294
You should have known.

08:57.753 --> 09:00.547
I got it. I'll fix your room right now.

09:00.714 --> 09:02.799
I'll do it myself. Just leave!

09:02.966 --> 09:06.970
I can't leave until I see that video with the
middle school girl!

09:07.137 --> 09:09.181
What did they offer you to lure you here?

09:09.890 --> 09:12.100
Iori! Got a minute?

09:13.518 --> 09:16.938
- Go ahead.
- You're staying here, so you should help.

09:17.230 --> 09:19.983
I'll fix your room just like you want it.

09:20.400 --> 09:22.194
I'm still worried...

09:25.113 --> 09:28.366
Hey, Kohei. Is this really going to be okay?

09:28.784 --> 09:30.243
IORI: "DON'T...
THE MOON IS WATCHING..."

09:30.827 --> 09:34.664
Yeah. If he's the exact opposite of me,
then this will be perfect.

09:36.374 --> 09:38.084
What's wrong, Iori Kitahara?

09:40.629 --> 09:43.173
You bastard! Stop!
Don't beat me up--

09:46.384 --> 09:48.553
This is worse than before!

09:48.720 --> 09:50.931
- What's on this DVD?
- Want to check it out?

09:51.097 --> 09:52.974
Are you even listening to me?

09:53.850 --> 09:54.851
Iori?

09:57.771 --> 09:59.356
What's wrong, Nanaka?

09:59.523 --> 10:01.107
I thought I'd help.

10:01.274 --> 10:04.861
- I'm fine right now.
- If it's about just now, I don't mind.

10:05.445 --> 10:08.240
I don't care if you're a guy.

10:08.573 --> 10:09.616
Really?

10:09.783 --> 10:11.952
To tell you the truth, I like you too...

10:14.246 --> 10:16.581
Nanaka. Just now, that was--

10:16.748 --> 10:19.626
Oh, sorry, Iori...

10:20.335 --> 10:23.880
I have to call my friend...

10:24.089 --> 10:26.383
Taku... Yusuke...

10:26.550 --> 10:30.887
My room's going to be perfect and
I'm going to that party!

10:33.640 --> 10:37.018
I have to get Nanaka to like my room!

10:37.811 --> 10:39.271
Do you have any ideas?

10:39.604 --> 10:43.233
Listen! Nanaka's always fawning over her little sister
Chisa.

10:43.400 --> 10:44.401
Really?

10:44.568 --> 10:47.404
In other words, Nanaka likes rooms that are...

10:48.947 --> 10:52.033
Hey. This isn't quite right.

10:52.409 --> 10:54.911
Stop talking and get moving!

10:55.370 --> 10:58.164
This looks like a stalker's room.

10:59.457 --> 11:02.002
It's almost time for the drinking party.

11:02.669 --> 11:04.254
I forgot to tell you.

11:04.796 --> 11:08.174
Something came up and they want to postpone.

11:10.176 --> 11:12.345
- Postpone?
- Postpone.

11:13.221 --> 11:15.807
- It's not today?
- It's not today.

11:16.433 --> 11:17.809
Hold on.

11:18.059 --> 11:20.604
That means that everything we did today was--

11:20.937 --> 11:22.439
Iori. Want some tea?

11:37.996 --> 11:39.456
Iori, isn't that great?

11:39.623 --> 11:42.709
This room lets you live an independent lifestyle.

11:42.876 --> 11:45.795
This isn't what I was hoping for!

11:45.962 --> 11:47.923
HE WAS THEN ISOLATED
IN A DETACHED ROOM.

11:48.089 --> 11:48.965
Grand Blue Dreaming

11:53.261 --> 11:56.681
Me and Kotobuki are going to
take care of the freshmen.

11:57.432 --> 11:59.476
Why are you guys hanging out in my room?

12:01.186 --> 12:03.855
Because we've always used it as our club room.

12:04.022 --> 12:06.900
We can't change hang-out spots just because of you.

12:07.067 --> 12:10.612
I want to use my room how I want...

12:11.237 --> 12:12.489
Good morning.

12:12.781 --> 12:13.865
Hey.

12:14.449 --> 12:16.117
Good morning, Iori...

12:18.828 --> 12:21.498
You're wearing clothes today. Good job.

12:21.665 --> 12:23.750
What an unexpected compliment.

12:24.292 --> 12:25.627
Do you have a club activity?

12:25.919 --> 12:29.005
Yeah. I thought we'd do something with the freshmen.

12:29.422 --> 12:31.383
How many freshmen joined?

12:31.967 --> 12:33.927
Three for now.

12:35.303 --> 12:38.640
Freshmen, thanks for coming today!

12:38.807 --> 12:40.767
Three? You mean us?

12:41.101 --> 12:45.021
- Why are you here, Kohei?
- I got an urgent call from a senior.

12:45.188 --> 12:46.314
THE VOICE ACTOR, KAYA MIZUKI
IS COMING TO GRAND BLUE! MEET AT 10!

12:46.481 --> 12:47.524
This is Kaya.

12:47.732 --> 12:50.193
- They're lying, of course!
- Really!

12:50.360 --> 12:51.361
We were lying.

12:51.945 --> 12:55.156
Hey! How can you fall for such an obvious lie?

12:56.616 --> 12:58.743
He's crying for real? How old is he?

12:59.244 --> 13:03.039
Kaya is busy
and can't come for a while.

13:03.206 --> 13:06.001
You mean she used to come a lot?

13:06.167 --> 13:08.545
- Yeah. She used to come a lot.
- Really?

13:08.753 --> 13:11.715
- Yeah. Really!
- Celebrities come often too.

13:11.881 --> 13:14.509
I bet you're trying to trick us again.

13:15.301 --> 13:16.970
I wouldn't lie to you.

13:17.137 --> 13:19.305
I won't believe you without proof.

13:19.723 --> 13:22.308
Her wet suit is over there.

13:22.976 --> 13:24.561
Her wet suit?

13:24.978 --> 13:27.147
Can I do a tasting?

13:27.313 --> 13:30.191
Wow, that's what a pervert would say...

13:30.400 --> 13:32.318
I feel motivated now!

13:32.485 --> 13:34.279
Teach me about diving!

13:34.446 --> 13:35.947
Yeah. Leave it to us.

13:36.114 --> 13:38.575
Do I have to participate too?

13:39.784 --> 13:42.078
You're already experienced. You don't need to.

13:42.245 --> 13:44.122
Then I'm not going to participate.

13:44.289 --> 13:45.832
Chisa, you should participate.

13:45.999 --> 13:48.710
It's important to learn how beginners act.

13:50.378 --> 13:52.213
Can I just watch?

13:52.547 --> 13:54.507
What!? Are you sick?

13:54.841 --> 13:58.053
- No...
- Oh, so that's what you're talking about.

13:59.054 --> 14:01.848
I can't swim. So...

14:02.015 --> 14:05.185
- Don't worry about it.
- I do worry about it.

14:05.351 --> 14:07.312
There are divers who can't swim.

14:07.479 --> 14:09.230
But...

14:09.397 --> 14:12.358
Don't say no before you've even tried.

14:12.525 --> 14:13.735
That'd be a waste.

14:15.278 --> 14:16.863
Well, if you say so...

14:18.698 --> 14:19.866
So...

14:20.033 --> 14:22.827
We're going to practice swimming today.

14:22.994 --> 14:25.997
You said it doesn't matter that I can't swim!

14:26.456 --> 14:28.917
Swimming technique isn't that important.

14:29.084 --> 14:31.127
It's important to get used to the water.

14:32.587 --> 14:35.381
Let's hurry up and change into swimsuits!

14:36.466 --> 14:38.051
Do I have to change too?

14:38.510 --> 14:39.719
Of course.

14:41.221 --> 14:42.514
In other words...

14:42.972 --> 14:45.683
People who can't swim are afraid of the water.

14:45.850 --> 14:48.144
That's not good for diving.

14:48.353 --> 14:51.231
It's hard to focus. Can you put some pants on?

14:51.564 --> 14:55.944
If you're afraid of the water,
you might panic when you're in trouble.

14:56.236 --> 15:00.281
You won't be able to breathe efficiently,
and you'll use up more air.

15:01.032 --> 15:04.160
Your safety is on the line, so you'd better practice.

15:04.702 --> 15:08.164
I'm surprised...
You're serious when it comes to diving.

15:08.498 --> 15:10.416
Hurry up and change.

15:13.294 --> 15:14.963
Okay. Let's begin.

15:15.630 --> 15:17.715
Iori. Start with the basics.

15:17.882 --> 15:20.051
Practice opening your eyes underwater.

15:20.927 --> 15:22.512
Open my eyes underwater?

15:22.804 --> 15:25.515
Your feet can touch the bottom here. Relax and try it.

15:26.307 --> 15:27.517
Okay.

15:31.563 --> 15:32.647
It'll be okay...

15:32.814 --> 15:35.275
Opening my eyes should be easy...

15:40.655 --> 15:42.949
- You couldn't do it?
- Sorry.

15:43.158 --> 15:45.160
Then try using this.

15:47.954 --> 15:51.332
- Do you want to practice with gear too?
- Okay.

15:51.833 --> 15:54.210
You'll feel less scared that way.

15:54.711 --> 15:55.712
Okay.

15:59.632 --> 16:01.676
I hear something strange.

16:02.218 --> 16:04.554
I can't breathe. It's hard to move.

16:05.096 --> 16:07.056
But, there's no pressure on my eyes.

16:07.557 --> 16:09.350
The water's not coming in.

16:09.767 --> 16:11.603
Maybe I can open my eyes now...

16:18.735 --> 16:21.571
How was it? The view underwater is beautiful, right?

16:22.572 --> 16:25.825
I'll never be able to go underwater again...

16:26.326 --> 16:30.830
- What are you doing?
- Helping you stay calm in the case that gear comes off!

16:30.997 --> 16:32.707
Take off the goggles? Not the--

16:33.166 --> 16:34.918
Let's do this.

16:35.877 --> 16:37.629
You're fine in the bath, right?

16:37.921 --> 16:40.715
Yeah. I like baths.

16:46.387 --> 16:49.974
I get diving, but wearing a swimsuit in a pool?

17:03.279 --> 17:04.614
How was it, Iori?

17:06.491 --> 17:07.951
Hard to say...

17:10.578 --> 17:12.497
No! Wait!

17:12.664 --> 17:15.541
This is part of the training!
Right?

17:15.833 --> 17:19.545
- You really do like stripping down, don't you?
- Kotobuki!

17:20.755 --> 17:22.090
Pervert...

17:23.716 --> 17:25.635
I don't take pleasure in
exposing myself!

17:25.802 --> 17:27.595
I hope you can understand, Chisa!

17:27.762 --> 17:29.722
So, what are you doing?

17:29.889 --> 17:32.183
We're training Iori to get used to the water.

17:32.350 --> 17:34.435
Why won't you listen to me?

17:34.769 --> 17:37.730
For now, I'll just watch from over there.

17:37.897 --> 17:39.816
I'm not a pervert.

17:40.441 --> 17:42.110
All right Iori, let's continue.

17:42.277 --> 17:44.821
Keep trying to enjoy being underwater!

17:45.363 --> 17:46.823
Underwater...

17:49.659 --> 17:50.827
No.

17:50.994 --> 17:54.580
I'm not interested in going underwater anymore.

18:01.671 --> 18:03.423
How was it, Iori?

18:03.589 --> 18:05.216
Will you be able to enjoy diving?

18:05.383 --> 18:07.093
No. Not at all.

18:07.635 --> 18:09.804
Do you want to go out for a bit with me?

18:16.978 --> 18:19.063
Aquariums are nice at night, right?

18:19.230 --> 18:21.232
Yeah. It feels so mysterious.

18:21.941 --> 18:25.528
But, it's already closed.
How did you get them to let us in?

18:25.778 --> 18:28.698
Chisa-chan helps out here sometimes.

18:28.865 --> 18:31.117
- Help?
- Like that.

18:35.413 --> 18:37.373
Chisa does stuff like that...

18:41.461 --> 18:43.504
That's not how I imagined her.

18:43.796 --> 18:47.133
You don't have a good eye for people.

18:48.176 --> 18:50.803
Chisa-chan's really popular.

18:53.014 --> 18:55.433
Well, there are a lot of masochists out there...

18:55.600 --> 18:57.518
That's not what I'm talking about...

18:58.102 --> 18:59.562
Chisa-chan's a good girl.

18:59.729 --> 19:02.023
She can be awkward sometimes,

19:02.357 --> 19:04.692
but she's cute, kind, and soft.

19:04.859 --> 19:06.277
And she smells nice.

19:06.778 --> 19:08.946
I didn't know any of that.

19:11.074 --> 19:13.534
Maybe I should study fish too.

19:13.993 --> 19:15.286
Do you like them?

19:15.661 --> 19:19.290
I thought it would help me enjoy being underwater.

19:19.916 --> 19:21.918
Oh, I see.

19:24.295 --> 19:27.423
You're just thinking too much.

19:29.592 --> 19:30.843
Do you think so?

19:31.302 --> 19:34.430
Chisa-chan and I have
never thought about that before.

19:34.806 --> 19:37.934
That's because you're both
good at swimming and like fish.

19:38.101 --> 19:41.187
No. No one's born knowing how to swim.

19:41.354 --> 19:43.481
Or knowing lots about fish.

19:43.648 --> 19:46.317
I just want you to try feeling things at first.

19:47.026 --> 19:49.070
Feeling things? Feel what?

19:49.570 --> 19:52.365
Don't think about anything.

19:52.532 --> 19:55.952
Empty your mind,

19:56.702 --> 19:58.496
and feel the world underwater.

20:06.170 --> 20:07.505
It's amazing, right?

20:08.047 --> 20:10.550
So, this is the world underwater?

20:11.259 --> 20:14.846
No. This is just a world
that's similar to the world underwater.

20:16.139 --> 20:21.227
There are places where you can experience worlds
that are even more amazing than this.

20:21.936 --> 20:24.313
More amazing than this?

20:25.356 --> 20:30.153
To tell you the truth,
Chisa-chan is the one who told me to take you here.

20:30.778 --> 20:32.530
Chisa? Why?

20:33.448 --> 20:36.325
I bet she wants you to like diving.

20:37.535 --> 20:39.036
Why does she want that?

20:39.537 --> 20:41.539
She wants you to know.

20:42.290 --> 20:47.545
She wants you to know that a beautiful world exists
underwater.

20:48.171 --> 20:50.465
Tokita and Kotobuki feel the same way.

20:50.757 --> 20:53.801
That's why they keep pushing you to dive.

20:54.427 --> 20:55.803
I see...

20:56.345 --> 21:00.141
No one likes hearing people say
negative things about what they like.

21:00.933 --> 21:06.022
It's better to have more friends who
share the same interests.

21:06.606 --> 21:09.609
That way, it's more fun for me, and more fun for them.

21:10.651 --> 21:16.324
I also want you to know that even though
the water is scary, there's much more to it.

21:16.991 --> 21:18.367
Right...

21:19.535 --> 21:22.205
I feel more interested now...

21:23.915 --> 21:25.082
Really?

21:25.708 --> 21:27.793
I'm glad.

21:32.965 --> 21:35.051
- Chisa.
- What?

21:36.344 --> 21:37.845
Here. A souvenir.

21:38.679 --> 21:42.517
Do you have any idea
how many times I've been to that aquarium?

21:43.142 --> 21:46.521
- It's an expression of my gratitude.
- Gratitude?

21:46.938 --> 21:50.566
You asked Nanaka to take me there, right?

21:51.734 --> 21:54.654
I didn't want you to insult diving.

21:54.820 --> 21:57.031
I see. I'm going to try it out.

21:59.408 --> 22:01.369
- Well, then.
- Wait.

22:03.120 --> 22:05.540
- How was it?
- How was what?

22:06.249 --> 22:07.416
Underwater.

22:08.543 --> 22:09.710
Well...

22:09.877 --> 22:11.963
I still don't like it,

22:12.547 --> 22:14.924
but I want to get a closer look next time.

22:15.925 --> 22:16.926
Oh, really?

22:17.301 --> 22:19.095
That's why I got that present for you.

22:19.428 --> 22:20.930
Thanks, Chisa.

22:22.265 --> 22:23.307
Hold on.

22:27.103 --> 22:29.939
You should have gotten something cuter,

22:30.356 --> 22:31.566
idiot!

22:32.108 --> 22:33.442
DEEP BLUE AL FINE
KAYA MIZUKI

22:33.609 --> 22:35.695
Here’s your mic, Kitahara.

22:35.903 --> 22:39.949
Me, too...? All right, let’s do this!

22:40.241 --> 22:43.452
- Yeah, sing your heart out.
- You guys seem to be having fun.

22:45.121 --> 22:51.127
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.335 --> 22:57.049
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.258 --> 23:03.014
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:03.222 --> 23:09.312
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.520 --> 23:14.567
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.775 --> 23:22.158
Even if I were to lose everything
I’d still want you to know

23:22.366 --> 23:28.247
Trapped in the sky so far away
I’m praying with ripped off wings

23:28.456 --> 23:34.211
Because we span together
The vows of areppegio

23:34.420 --> 23:40.134
If life sparkles only to the beat
of the resonating stars

23:40.343 --> 23:43.137
I’ll sacrifice everything

23:43.346 --> 23:47.683
Till death do us apart

23:47.892 --> 23:49.769
Cheers!

23:54.565 --> 23:57.193
We’re very sorry!

24:02.281 --> 24:04.533
I drank too much again...

24:05.034 --> 24:06.202
Water...

24:07.036 --> 24:08.496
What are you doing?

24:13.417 --> 24:15.169
Let's sleep some more.

24:15.336 --> 24:16.921
NEXT EPISODE
"A NEW WORLD"
